      "writtenOn": "2018-03-26T22:14:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is handled in the charge state machine like this currently:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_BATTERY_REQUESTS_NIL_WHEN_DEAD\n\t\t\t/*\n\t\t\t * TODO (crosbug.com/p/29467): remove this workaround\n\t\t\t * for dead battery that requests no voltage/current\n\t\t\t */\n\t\t\tif (curr.requested_voltage \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026\n\t\t\t    curr.requested_current \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026\n\t\t\t    curr.batt.state_of_charge \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\t\t\t/* Battery is dead, give precharge current */\n\t\t\t\tcurr.requested_voltage \u003d\n\t\t\t\t\tbatt_info-\u003evoltage_max;\n\t\t\t\tcurr.requested_current \u003d\n\t\t\t\t\tbatt_info-\u003eprecharge_current;\n\t\t\t} else\n#endif\n\nI put this in Coral so that batteries that need this can use it without applying it to all batteries.",
